-- title:
--   Powers of (X₀,X₁) in W[[X₀,X₁]] via low-degree coefficients
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring, let $e$ be a natural number, and let $g$ be a formal power series in two variables over $W$, i.e. an element of `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) W`, the power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ indexed by `Fin 2`. The assertion is an equivalence: $g$ belongs to the $e$-th power of the ideal generated by the two variables, $(\mathrm{span}\{X_0,X_1\})^e$, if and only if for every exponent vector $n \colon \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to_{f} \mathbb{N}$ with $n(0) + n(1) < e$ the coefficient of $g$ at $n$ vanishes. In other words, the $e$-th power of the maximal-variable ideal consists exactly of those series all of whose monomials have total degree at least $e$. No hypotheses beyond commutativity of $W$ are imposed; in particular $W$ need not be local, noetherian or nontrivial, and the degenerate case $e = 0$ is included, where both sides hold vacuously.
--
--   This identifies the adic filtration of the two-variable power series ring by the ideal of the variables with the filtration by total degree. It is used throughout the analysis of local charts of the Drinfeld curve, for instance in the study of ring automorphisms of $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ and their linear parts, and in the rigidification of special formal schemes in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_mem_span_X_pow_iff_forall_coeff_eq_zero_of_degree_lt.lean

import Mathlib
